I wrote two task files and the issue responses, and committed them as 5ac43fa0. Neither task touches the providers code, because 7 of the last 13 self-driven diffs went there and the trajectory warning said to send this session's slot elsewhere.

Task 1: Part of #1094. Use yoagent's ReadLog so the "don't overwrite a file you only half-read" guard is tracked per agent. Right now read_file and write_file are built without a log, so yoagent's version of the guard never runs. yoyo's own guard keeps one record for the whole process. That causes two bugs: a sub-agent's full read lets the parent overwrite a file it only partly read (item 3), and a file shrunk by bash after a partial read is judged only by its line count (item 4).
• The plan gives the parent and each sub-agent its own log.
• It keeps partial_read_guard.rs running alongside, because yoagent records reads before yoyo's output truncation cuts them. Removing yoyo's guard would bring back the truncated-page bug (item 2).
• Tests: run the item 3 and item 4 cases on HEAD first and confirm they fail, then pin the allowed cases. The control is to remove the log and check that exactly those two tests go red.
• It stays "Part of": item 1 (overwriting an existing file that was never read) is still an undecided product choice.

Task 2: Part of #1127. In the shell, yoyo blame and yoyo ast print yoyo <verb> usage, while the REPL keeps /<verb>. It follows the earlier grep/def/outline fix (command_form(surface, verb)). The REPL text stays as it is because it's correct where it's shown. The integration test that currently pins the wrong /blame shell text gets updated. docs, lint, risk, skill, map and memories remain for later.

Issue responses: there were no community issues today. The provider-list tickets (#1147, #1118, #1121, #1012) are deferred because of the concentration warning. I skipped the umbrella review: #1012 already has slices 2 and 3 decided by the owner, and #1064 has a per-sink done-when. A release isn't due.

session_plan/ is gitignored, so I committed it with git add -f. That also committed assessment.md, which earlier phases had left on disk only.
